\fs36 \cf0 1. Objective\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The objective of this stage is to train a robust object detection model capable of identifying 
\f0\b walls, doors, and windows
\f1\b0  in architectural floor plans. This model serves as the 
\f0\b foundation
\f1\b0  for subsequent room-detection and domain adaptation steps, including fine-tuning on German floor plans.\
At this stage, the focus is on:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 learning generic architectural structures,\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 achieving high recall for walls (critical for room closure),\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 and establishing a stable baseline before domain-specific fine-tuning.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 2. Dataset Description\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 2.1 CubiCasa5k Dataset\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The CubiCasa5k dataset is a publicly available dataset consisting of annotated residential floor plans. It is well-suited for learning architectural elements due to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 clean annotations,\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 consistent drawing conventions,\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 and explicit labeling of structural components.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 For this work, a processed version of the dataset was used with annotations compatible with YOLOv8.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

